ntial. Show-off vs egocentric vs nasty remarks vs hot temper. All are concerns.\n\nWe might need to ask other agents for missing info, e.g., about candidate's crew cooperation or stress resilience specifics. But we need to make a contribution now. Could start by presenting candidate A's strengths and concerns, and propose provisional recommendation for candidate A, but note concerns. Or we could propose candidate C due to decision quality and calmness, but note communication issues.\n\nGiven we need to start discussion, we can state our current recommendation: Candidate C, because of quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical understanding, which are top for long-distance flights. Acknowledge concerns about communication and egocentric but propose that these can be mitigated.\n\nLet's do that. Provide evidence: \"makes correct decisions quickly\", \"keeps calm in a crisis\", \"understands complicated technology\". Concerns: \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"regarded as egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\". Explain why strengths outweigh concerns relative to other candidates.\n\nThus vote for Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
