blem solving, concentration) are valuable, but concerns (hot temper, know-it-all) raise crew cooperation issues. Compare D to B and C. Might suggest D as a viable alternative, or argue that D's concerns outweigh strengths, so still C is best.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Considering the evidence: C has strong decision quality, calmness, technical competence, but communication issues. B has reliability, stress handling, but weak memory for numbers (attention risk) and uncooperative. D has responsibility, problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all, and no evidence of crew cooperation. A is not discussed much.\n\nGiven the new info, perhaps we can argue that D's hot temper and know-it-all are serious for crew cooperation, making D less suitable. So we maintain C as leading.\n\nThus we will state we still recommend Candidate C, but note that D's profile shows some strengths but also serious crew cooperation concerns, and we need more evidence on D's crew cooperation before considering.\n\nWe must reference prior discussion: Agent 3's argument about B's weak memory for numbers, and Agent 2's lack of evidence on D. We'll say that D's lack of crew cooperation evidence and hot temper make him less suitable than C.\n\nThus vote Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
