{"id": 33, "ts": 1779736377.7042258, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f1\u2019s conclusion that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit, especially given his proven \u201cquick correct decisions,\u201d \u201ccalm in a crisis,\u201d and \u201cunderstanding of complicated technology.\u201d Those attributes directly satisfy the decision\u2011quality, stress\u2011resilience, and technical\u2011competence criteria that are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fAt the same time, we still have not examined Candidate\u202fA, whose profile could affect our final decision.\u202fMy notes show that Candidate\u202fA \u201ccan anticipate dangerous situations,\u201d \u201csees complex connections,\u201d has \u201cexcellent spatial vision,\u201d and possesses \u201cvery good leadership qualities.\u201d These strengths suggest high operational reliability, strong situational awareness, and the ability to guide a crew effectively.\u202fHowever, he is also \u201cregarded as a show\u2011off\u201d and \u201cnot open to new ideas,\u201d which raise concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability\u2014areas where Candidate\u202fC already shows potential weaknesses.\u202fGiven that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s critical safety\u2011critical strengths are documented and his communication issues appear more manageable than Candidate\u202fA\u2019s apparent attitude problems, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fC, while urging us to discuss Candidate\u202fA\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation and adaptability in more detail before we close.", "thoughts": "We need to produce the public message and metadata JSON as per instructions. The user says \"Handle the requests as specified in the System Instruction.\" That is a meta instruction. We should continue the meeting. We are Agent 2 (Markus Weber). We need to respond to the latest turn, which is Agent 1's public message (the last one